"'`ops.go:409–449` first commits wrapper restoration, then reads the CREATE-time binding and requires its generation to equal the new mutation context. `TestReviewRestoreAcrossServerGeneration` persists the prior binding, changes CurrentGeneration and the request to `generation-after-reboot`, and drives Execute(restore). The production runner receives `new-session`, then restore fails with `terminal_backend_integrity_failure at restore binding image`. §4.C line 1211 explicitly requires prior binding, Checkpoint, and **new binding** evidence; §4.E line 1387 and §4.2 require restoration after reboot. Re-reading the old binding only solves the nil result within the old generation. Compose the binding owner to persist/return the correct successor, validate before irreversible effects where possible, and prove retry/crash recovery across a real generation change.

